  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The length of the perpendicular from the origin, on normal to the curve, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, at the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, is.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wVuKA",
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JzJ5x",
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SPqZ2",
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "HnjvH",
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Differentiate the above curve,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>So, at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p><p>So, equation of normal to the curve at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p>Thus, perpendicular distance from origin on the normal is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>.</p>",
